		(uuid "489279f5-8167-4219-95c0-2be37b89cb79")
		(at 504.501236 217.943129 90)
		(descr "Panasonic AXK680337YG P5K-series 80-pin/0.5mm-pitch board-to-board HEADER, 3.0mm mated height. Real dimensions from Panasonic/Mouser's own P5K/P5KS catalog PDF (mouser.com/catalog/specsheets/AXK.pdf), read directly: body 23.20 x 4.60mm (A x width), pin field 19.50mm (B, = (40-1)*0.5mm exactly). Land pattern real: 40 pins/row x 2 rows, 0.5mm pitch, rows staggered by 0.25mm (half pitch, per the catalog's own 'Recommended PC board pattern' drawing), pad 0.25 x 0.75mm, total footprint span 5.60mm (consistent across every land-pattern drawing in the catalog). Pin numbering (1-80 sequential by row) is an ASSUMED convention, not independently verified against a real pin-1 diagram -- the catalog's own orientation key is a chamfered body corner (reproduced here on F.SilkS near pin 1) rather than a numbered pinout drawing. Mates with the ALINX AC7200 module's own AXK580137YG sockets (module-side part number CONFIRMED via ALINX's real schematic, docs/AC7200_Schematic.pdf page 12) -- see ../AC7200/AC7200_README.md.")
